--- body ---
## Context

The journal model set locked by ticket 0175 (`[sets.modelset_ablation_journal]`
in `experiments/experiments.toml:162-185`) has two flagship choices that need
revision before the 0177 sweep runs:

**Qwen flagship**: pairs three `qwen3.6-*` siblings (`27b`, `35b-a3b`, `plus`)
with `qwen/qwen3-max` as the flagship — one generation behind the family.

**Anthropic flagship**: uses `anthropic/claude-opus-4.7` — user directs swap
to `anthropic/claude-opus-4.6` (no rationale recorded; presume more stable /
cheaper / better-characterised for the baseline).

Verification (2026-05-20, OpenRouter `/api/v1/models`):

```
$ curl -s https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models | jq -r '.data[].id | select(test("qwen.*max"))'
qwen/qwen3.6-max-preview
qwen/qwen3-max-thinking
qwen/qwen3-max

$ curl -s https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models | jq -r '.data[].id | select(test("claude.*opus"))'
anthropic/claude-opus-4.7-fast
anthropic/claude-opus-4.7
anthropic/claude-opus-4.6-fast
anthropic/claude-opus-4.6
anthropic/claude-opus-4.5
anthropic/claude-opus-4.1
anthropic/claude-opus-4
```

Both `qwen/qwen3.6-max-preview` and `anthropic/claude-opus-4.6` are live.

## Impact on downstream tickets

- **0177 (this sweep)**: blocked on 0180. Sweep should rerun after 0180 lands.
- **Experiment 2** ("deep research vs parametric" within-model claim): the
  intended within-family pair is `qwen3-max` ↔ `qwen3-max-thinking`. If
  0180 *replaces* qwen3-max with qwen3.6-max-preview, Exp 2 loses that
  pair unless qwen3-max stays in the registry (it can stay in models.yaml
  without being in the journal set).

## Actions

1. **models.yaml**:
   - Add `qwen/qwen3.6-max-preview` (verified prices from `/api/v1/models`).
   - Verify `anthropic/claude-opus-4.6` is already in models.yaml; add if
     missing with verified prices.
   - Annotate provider, country, architecture, context window, size_class
     for any new entry. Reference: existing entries follow a consistent
     YAML shape.
2. **experiments.toml** `[sets.modelset_ablation_journal]`:
   - Swap `anthropic/claude-opus-4.7` → `anthropic/claude-opus-4.6`.
   - For Qwen flagship: decide between **augment** (16 → 17 models, both
     qwen3-max and qwen3.6-max-preview kept — preserves Exp 2 pair) and
     **replace** (swap qwen3-max → qwen3.6-max-preview). Augment is the
     safer default; +5 reps at ~$0.30. Surface the choice to the human
     in the ticket log before executing.
3. Re-run the parametric baseline sweep on the corrected set under a new
   ticket (call it 0181-rerun-experiment-1-sweep). Commit bd46943
   (manager+worker silent-drop fixes) is a prerequisite — must be merged
   to main before the rerun.
4. 0178 manuscript annex notes the 0175 → 0180 → 0181 chain so reviewers
   understand the model-set version.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `anthropic/claude-opus-4.6` present in `models.yaml` with verified prices
- [ ] `qwen/qwen3.6-max-preview` present in `models.yaml` with verified prices
- [ ] `[sets.modelset_ablation_journal]` updated:
      Anthropic flagship → 4.6;
      Qwen flagship per recorded augment/replace decision (log the reasoning here)
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes (no schema or test regressions)
- [ ] 0181 rerun ticket created (depends-on: 0180, bd46943-PR merged)
- [ ] 0178 manuscript annex notes the model-set revision

## Notes

- Discovered during 0177 (run-experiment-1-sweep). The 0177 mission spec
  explicitly forbade reconfiguring model IDs ("0175 locked them"), so the
  fix-up belongs in this separate ticket.
- The four silent-drop fixes in commit bd46943 (model_set / seed / max_tokens
  / modules_dir) are a prerequisite for any future sweep against this set.
  Currently on branch t0177, separate PR.
- "preview" suffix: OpenRouter sometimes deprecates `:preview` slugs once a
  GA variant ships. Worth checking quarterly; if `qwen/qwen3.6-max` (no
  preview) lands, switch to that in the same ticket cycle.
- Opus 4.7 stays in models.yaml as a retired flagship reference; only the
  journal-set membership changes.
